From 382fdf18e1934c72e0cfcc0b0e578c58d80dd2f6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dixonSolutions <203963471+dixonSolutions@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 19:47:43 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 12/18] console: Do not touch gd->jt before jumptable_init()

input_stdio_register() reassigns stdin when the registered device matches
the "stdin" variable. With stdin=button-kbd that happens in
stdio_add_devices(), before jumptable_init() has allocated gd->jt, and
console_setfile() faulted writing gd->jt->getc (synchronous abort, far
0x8). On the SM-T570 this reset U-Boot a few seconds after start.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 common/console.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/common/console.c b/common/console.c
index dafea373..23b29784 100644
--- a/common/console.c
+++ b/common/console.c
@@ -195,7 +195,13 @@ static int console_setfile(int file, struct stdio_dev * dev)
 		/*
 		 * Update monitor functions
 		 * (to use the console stuff by other applications)
+		 *
+		 * An input device registered from stdio_add_devices() can be
+		 * assigned here (input_stdio_register() with a matching
+		 * "stdin") before jumptable_init() has allocated gd->jt.
 		 */
+		if (!gd->jt)
+			break;
 		switch (file) {
 		case stdin:
 			gd->jt->getc = getchar;
-- 
